                        "entry_id": "ba8a55a2-559a-38b8-b2b2-bde607b52f85",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The history and genealogy of demigods or heroes, especially the uncompleted history found in portions of Hesiod's Theogony."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3418a018-71db-4dd8-80c9-091bb82ed6f6",
                                "sense_id": "6252ca27-cf30-31fd-99e6-dd5a57af7585",
                                "text": "[…] the last portion, which is in fact a heroogony, being an account of the heroes born by mortal morthers whose charms had drawn the immortals from Olympus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd3abc13-c0d9-4dc3-9cdd-6ec8dcb3eb1f",
                                "sense_id": "6252ca27-cf30-31fd-99e6-dd5a57af7585",
                                "text": "The Theogony consists of a cosmogony, a theogony proper, and an unfinished heroogony."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6cb59342-0216-4a74-be62-221f78a68c94",
                                "sense_id": "6252ca27-cf30-31fd-99e6-dd5a57af7585",
                                "text": "Whether or not Hesiod added it himself, it should be no surprise that at the end of the Theogony there is a short heroogony (937f)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
